#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:29
#: 840c843d6d23450792d047facd3e1984
msgid "DroneCAN Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:31
#: 0d2ac964c5464409966f21b2667d3e09
msgid "DroneCAN ESCs setup is described on the :ref:`DroneCAN ESCs Autopilot Setup <common-uavcan-escs>` page but in short set the following parameters on the autopilot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:33
#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:75
#: cce94e51a65240b9b8217a2dddfc4f8c
#: 31fa94e8b0f0432ebfbdc9f9c89ce5ca
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER <CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1 (First driver) to specify that the ESCs are connected to the CAN1 port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:34
#: 77f7b908f3fd4166a934e7d90a0b18ad
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL <CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 1 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:38
#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:80
#: 1a95bfa4ff7740b9b998de42d56cd461
#: d8b424bdf5d240168d510de255a1f295
msgid "Set ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` to each motor channel (e.g. 33 - 40 for motors 1 - 8). This is automatically configured when setting frame class/type. If a motor channel isn't assigned to a servo output, commands won't be sent to the associated ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:41
#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:88
#: 197be1b7ffd94b59af3be7210b95636d
#: 7203f0f46b0a4ae8ba6dbe51250f5b6f
msgid "ESC Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:43
#: 75858f4bc4914abe8af5fd2ff7606bef
msgid "The ESCs can be configured using the :ref:`DroneCAN GUI Tool <common-uavcan-gui>` or `DroneCAN Web Tool <https://can.ardupilot.org/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:45
#: 432a17745e434382b325771386bef02e
msgid "To configure the ESC to receive commands from ``SERVOx`` output, set ``dronecan.escIndex`` to ``x - 1`` (e.g. for ``SERVO5``, set ``escIndex`` = 4). Note that this is different to PiccoloCAN, where motor channels are assigned to node ids, rather than servo output channels to the ``escIndex``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:46
#: 1287e4811c88483791a52459088c786f
msgid "Telemetry periods can be configured with the ``dronecan.messagePeriods`` settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:47
#: 11527bed297440f1bee9905980473d2b
msgid "By default, the ESC respects arming messages from the Autopilot. To always software enable the ESC when a command is received, and ignore arming messages, set ``config.swInhibit`` = 1 (False)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:49
#: b4b519e329c446f194b433127efeb6a1
msgid "By default, the Velocity ESC is configured to use Dynamic Node id Allocation (DNA). ``dronecan.nodeId`` should be set to \"0\" (to use DNA), unless all devices on the CAN bus are configured to use static IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:51
#: a29107040d344db9a697f989d47b9811
msgid "Only the DroneCAN specific settings are shown when fetching settings using the DroneCAN protocol. The full suite of Velocity ESC settings can be configured by enabling the ``show_advanced`` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:55
#: 8c8b13aa52734342b2b3e9e266b6f3be
msgid "It is recommended to configure your motor, and perform ESC and motor validation using PiccoloCAN with CEquip, and swap to DroneCAN, if required, during vehicle integration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:58
#: b3039243968e44d2b4d1b0880fb659e5
msgid "PiccoloCAN Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:60
#: f1c0c6580ce44b6c90b7b37e587536ed
msgid "The Velocity ESC supports the PiccoloCAN protocol. Originally developed for the Piccolo autopilot, the protocol is now natively supported by ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:62
#: c04a2ccd7062496ebcc16adbf3f303af
msgid "Support for PiccoloCAN is available by default in ArduPilot 4.7 (and lower).  If using ArduPilot 4.8 (and higher) please use the custom build server to create a firmware with the 'AP_PICCOLOCAN_ENABLED' build option enabled which can be done using the `Custom Build Server <https://custom.ardupilot.org/add_build>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:68
#: 6163f2e8c0174dc497c35c7f5777e5d3
msgid "More instructions on using the :ref:`Custom Build Server can be found here <common-custom-firmware>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:71
#: b26bda60313b4cb48e6755252b70600d
msgid "ArduPilot Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:73
#: 6259d00f3aaa4bbc9d63e287a71de97b
msgid "To enable communication with the Velocity ESCs using PiccoloCAN, the following parameters must be set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:76
#: 5edbbb90009c453195d983dd7b5c2695
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL <CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 4 (PiccoloCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:82
#: 3301d65f71cc4f4e82257a65585341e2
msgid "By default, all configured motor channels are used to send control commands to Velocity ESCs. These control messages are transmitted by the autopilot at a default rate of 50Hz. These parameters can be modified using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:84
#: 5623c39a01334d54ad8fdb64ad9c7ce8
msgid "The :ref:`CAN_D1_PC_ESC_BM <CAN_D1_PC_ESC_BM>` parameter is a bitmask that determines which ESC (motor) channels are transmitted over CAN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:85
#: 2498600a6e594729917ab1f59141fde7
msgid "The :ref:`CAN_D1_PC_ESC_RT <CAN_D1_PC_ESC_RT>` parameter determines the rate (Hz) at which commands are sent out to the connected Velocity ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:90
#: a3b0e659f3024648b58e6d5664a7a5e7
msgid "The following configuration settings should be used on the Velocity ESC for operation with Ardupilot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:92
#: 08d229f936814c6497f220ff996671fc
msgid "Set Piccolo Node ID to the motor channel the ESC should listen to. Note this may not be the same as the configured servo output number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:93
#: d53d926804bd47d18cd27ceca7549aba
msgid "Enable ``Listen for Broadcast Commands``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:96
#: ff9a238d4ebe4c3c8bf390703ed64351
msgid "Logging and Reporting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:98
#: 90703e55397f4a6d887691f7214a3b71
msgid "Velocity ESCs provide comprehensive telemetry information back to the autopilot which is recorded in the autopilot's onboard log, and can be viewed in any :ref:`ArduPilot compatible log viewer <common-logs>`.  This information includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:100
#: a3a3d4f75ca64ded83afa7c973077192
msgid "RPM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:101
#: f5d0c7d251824dd39fe8ee7dddc0cce3
msgid "Voltage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:102
#: bb2bd492b63143ffbf3398c879a540fd
msgid "ESC Temperature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:103
#: 8a69c8e9f5994d6d90ac8b9f1c6bfec3
msgid "Motor current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:104
#: f73e129fe0f04d248d95312e62048281
msgid "Motor Temperature (when used with an external sensor)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:106
#: 532eb7cafb7c4c6ca72986196c37ab4b
msgid "This information (except the motor temperature) can also be viewed in real-time using a ground station.  If using the Mission Planner go to the Flight Data screen's status tab and look for (e.g.) esc1_rpm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-velocity-can-escs.rst:114
#: 47c462e6a701407da063a2e77ecffa66
msgid "Sending ESC data to the GCS requires using MAVLink2.  Please check the appropriate SERIALx_PROTOCOL parameter is 2 (where \"x\" is the serial port number used for the telemetry connection)."
msgstr ""
